// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). One storyline: Sofia leaves her small rented
// room in Mustamäe, finds a flat in Kalamaja, moves in and learns the new part of town; her brother Jaan, colleagues
// Markus, Anna and Liis, uncle Viktor and mother Helgi help or visit. Goal, said on the first sheet: at the end the
// learner invites Sofia's family to her housewarming (soolaleivapidu) — the new home described and the way from the
// station explained (014 Kasuta).
//   011 viewing flats — adjective suffixes -ne/-line, -kas, -lik, -tu, eba- (valgusküllane, ruumikas, ebamugav…),
//       where things are (akna juures, voodi kohal); three ads; Kalamaja or Pelgulinn — a family council, the owner.
//   012 moving day — kus? kuhu? kust? (autosse, elutuppa, garaažist, perenaise juurest); Sofia's voice message, the
//       story of the day, the house rules from the neighbour; where did you put my things?
//   013 the new part of town — places and kuhu-forms (apteeki, raamatukokku, turule); the neighbours' cards, a walk with
//       Liis; Helgi is worried — is Kalamaja safe? (suffixes again: rahulik, lärmakas, ohutu).
//   014 asking and giving the way — mine / minge, kuni …-ni; to the health centre with Anna; a tourist and Viktor;
//       the housewarming: Helgi's and Viktor's messages, the call from the station, the invitation, the tour of the home.
// Module 2's words come back in the story (pere, vend, onu, oma, kaotama, unustama, omanik, ettepanek, eelistama,
// kokku leppima, traditsioon, lauamäng, abivalmis, rahul …). B1 grammar added here (METHODOLOGY_STANDARD §7): adjective
// suffixes -line, -kas, -lik, -tu, eba- (taught in 011, again in 013 and 014). Lesson 5 is the module's mini Harno A2
// exam (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b1/module03.js, the v1 file in archive/v1/b1/module03.js.
